// ═══ da010: VERTICAL SCALE + THE WING ═════════════════════════════════════
// Josh: the mountains need real altitude, and he wants to launch off them and
// glide. Those are one job, because a wing is only worth having if there is
// height to spend.
//
// ON SCALE, HONESTLY. da009 put the peaks at TRUE 1:1 (0.18 world units per
// metre vertical against 0.169 horizontal) and that IS geometrically correct.
// It also reads flat, and the reason is not a bug: a real mountain seen from
// a real distance genuinely subtends a shallow angle. Diablo from 10 km is
// about 6.7 degrees. Through a game camera that is a bump. Nearly every game
// that wants mountains to FEEL like mountains exaggerates vertical 1.5x to
// 3x, and this is why. _BAY_VSCALE is that exaggeration, applied about the
// WATERLINE so the coastline, the bridges and every road stay pinned exactly
// where the projection put them. Only the air above the water stretches.
